    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d474">

                <pb facs="0606" n="521" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg521"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.73/13: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Chargé in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bliss</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract<anchor n="65" xml:id="d474-f1"
                    />]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-01-25T13:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 25,
                                1919, 1 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>7126. Your 6674 [<hi rendition="#italic">6774</hi>].<anchor n="66"
                        xml:id="d474-f2"/> …</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
                <p>The application for concession by the Societe Coloniale has been fully dealt with
                    by Department in note to French Chargé and summary cabled to you in Department’s
                        7043.<anchor n="67" xml:id="d474-f3"/></p>
                <p>The Department reserves for later discussion the question of the landing of the
                    German cable.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
